;; Pay-off per search surface, PER PROBLEM AREA.
;;
;; Design (Joe, 2026-07-30): "pay-off per surface would, in a more sophisticated
;; model, be pay-off-per-surface per problem class. We have evidence that arXiv
;; was useful before; the fact that it wasn't used this time presumably means it
;; wasn't needed. More broadly arXiv is kind of the fall-through of a cond — if
;; all else fails, the answer should be in there, even if it's potentially more
;; expensive to search for it."
;;
;; The packet's rule 2 now encodes exactly that cond:
;;   (a) components — Loogle / LeanSearch, when the route is already known
;;   (b) Zulip archive — prior formalization and known Mathlib obstacles
;;   (c) arXiv — FALL-THROUGH, for when there is no route at all
;;
;; CRITICAL DISTINCTION this ledger must preserve, and the reason a global
;; hit-rate would mislead: a surface that was NOT NEEDED is not a surface that
;; FAILED. Recording only "arXiv: no anchor" would slowly build a false case
;; against the most expensive and most complete surface. So every row carries
;; :arms-tried, :arm-that-paid, and :not-needed separately.
;;
;; :area is the terrain pattern the row sits in — the same 7 patterns the memory
;; corpus is organised by — so this can be grouped by area once n is meaningful.
;; FIELD SHAPE (Joe, 2026-07-30): this began as a boolean :route-known-at-start?
;; and that was the wrong shape. A closer MAY inherit a likely route from a
;; previous session that ran out of time, but that should not be the typical
;; case -- deferring work that could have been closed directly is lazy for a
;; closer. So the field is :suggested-route, optional and free-text, carrying a
;; route only when one genuinely exists, plus :suggested-route-source so we can
;; tell an inherited plan from one the runner found itself.
;;
;; Note run 1's route came from the FILE's own docstring, not from a previous
;; session -- the mechanism already works informally, which is an argument for
;; wiring it explicitly rather than inventing it.
;;
;; It is NOT meaningful yet: n = 2.

